codex
The hash gate passed, the full required source range and Appendix II have been read from rendered page images, and the frozen census rerun is underway. The emerging source picture is important: Appendix II starts from Moh’s six-row table and eliminates those cases afterward; it does not explain the missing pre-table restriction. I’m now stress-testing the few genuinely source-derived candidates—especially the full factor-multiplicity data behind Proposition 4.6/5.3 and the top-radius inequality—against all six printed rows and the 652 excess rows.
