codex
A concrete discriminator has now emerged from the source, not from curve-fitting. Conditions (9)–(11) determine the multiplicity class of the zero root of each \(p(\pi)\). Proposition 5.6 applies to every major tower, including the unselected zero-root branch: if the zero root is unavoidably major at every descent, it produces the forbidden pure bottom root. At \((75,50)\), the forced zero multiplicities are \(20,3,2,0,9\) for \(M_2=5,10,40,55,60\); only \(M_2=55\) can omit the zero root, exactly matching Moh’s table. I’m implementing this as a branch-tree (“zero path”) condition now; this is materially stronger than the earlier rowwise NOT-ALL-(11) shadow.
