The two independent implementations now agree: universal major-factor closure preserves all six printed rows and reduces the discrepancy from 652 to 17 excess rows; the exact local ODE nondegeneracy reduces it further to 14. Neither Moh’s prose nor Appendix II states the remaining root-position realizability test, so I’m checking whether Appendix I’s differential equation supplies a valid finite numerical discriminator or only a bounded residual OPEN.
