+## 2. Numbered-claim hostile review
+
+### Claim (1)
+
+**CONFIRMED, with the two terminology repairs above.**  The independent image
+transcription agrees with charged §1.2, and (1.1) re-derives its p.188 identity.
+Source locators: Def.5.1(1)--(4), p.179; Prop.5.3, pp.180--183; Prop.5.5 proof,
+pp.187--188; search (8)--(13), p.201, lower two-thirds.  Promote the formulas,
+the $A$-dictionary, and the identity.  Do not promote “bottom polynomial” as
+a single global object, or $M_4=n-1$ as an enumerated effective datum.
+
+### Claim (2)
+
+**CONFIRMED.**  Algebraically, if
+$Q=V_r d_{r-1}/d_r=\triangle A+\square$, then
+
+\[
+V_{r-1}\le\triangle
+\iff A V_{r-1}\le Q,
+\]
+
+which is exactly the calibration lane's reconstructed (10).  The frozen rerun
+checked 521,190 level/assignment pairs and found no disagreement
+([run log](../box/mohprog-drivers-20260903/run_all-root.log), lines 755--758).
+Equation (1.1) turns (12)/(13) into the calibration endpoint congruence; the
+rerun checked 242,099 assignments in both directions with zero discrepancies
+(log lines 746--753).  Promote both equivalences, with the repair that the
+endpoint is Moh's separate (12)/(13), not “(10) at $r=1$.”
+
+### Claim (3)
+
+**CONFIRMED as a count; GAP in the word “true.”**  The exact frozen copies of
+`run_all.py` and `moh_skeleton_full.py` produced
+
+```text
+48 <= D <= 120: 1,692 V-assignments / 1,189 groups
+calibration without (11): 329 / 287
+1,189 / 287 = 4.142857...
+```
+
+The cross-control appears at log lines 766--773 and the rebased total at
+lines 775--806.  Thus restoring (11) really costs 4.14x in groups.  Promotion
+repair: call 1,692/1,189 the `PATH-ARITH(1--13)` space, not the true
+polynomial-admissible or complete-program space.
+
+### Claim (4)
+
+**CONFIRMED, with a correction to the charged hand calculation.**  At
+$(n,m,M_2,M_3,V_3)=(75,50,55,73,4)$, Def.5.1(3) gives
+
+\[
+\delta_2={1\over5},\qquad
+\delta_1=1-{5(20V_2-25)\over125V_2-25}.
+\]
+
+Thus $V_2=3$ gives $1/2$ and $V_2=2$ gives $2/3$, while the table prints
+$[1/3]$ for the latter.  Solving the displayed equation for
+$\delta_1=1/3$ gives $V_2=13/2$, **not** the charged report's $-1/2$.
+The conclusion is unchanged: no integral $V_2$ realizes it.  A fresh
+enumerator, independent of the frozen module, found 682 (1)--(7) arithmetic
+assignments at $(75,50)$ and zero with $\delta_1=1/3$; its complete result is
+[`independent-75-50.json`](../box/mohprog-drivers-20260903/independent-75-50.json).
+Promote the erratum $1/3\mapsto2/3$ and nonattainment; repair the intermediate
+value to $13/2$.
+
+### Claim (5)
+
+**CONFIRMED computational core; REFUTED as stated if “(1)--(13)” includes its
+semantic premises; OPEN as an assertion about Moh's lost program.**  The
+frozen rerun gives exactly 658 rows, 508 groups, and 63 $(n,m)$ classes; all
+six p.202 rows survive (log lines 32--69 and 74--736).  A separately written
+enumerator agrees on 658/63.  Moh says at p.202, first paragraph, that his
+program “produces only” the displayed exceptions, namely six expanded rows
+in four degree classes.  The numerical discrepancy is therefore real.
+
+What the discrepancy proves is narrower than charged §5 says.  It proves
+that the path-only arithmetic translation of the displayed formulas is not
+the output procedure behind the table.  It does **not** prove that a hidden
+scalar predicate was present: condition (4) already says “is ...
+characteristic data,” Props.5.3/5.6 impose a whole-tree closure on that phrase,
+and the surviving 14 may reflect still unencoded realization data.  A program
+error or an incompletely reported search is also observationally possible
+because no source or listing of Moh's CDC 6500 program is present.
+
+The charged `NOT-ALL-(11)` numerical shadow is not exact.  Equation (11) is a
+necessary congruence for a typed zero factor, not a declaration that the
+factor is zero; a value may satisfy both (10) and (11).  Prop.5.6 forbids a
+*typed* all-zero bottom point (pp.188--189).  The source-safe projection is a
+recursive forced-zero test, not “reject every row whose numbers satisfy (11)
+at all levels.”  See §3.3.  Promotion: retain 658/63 as a named arithmetic
+superset and retain the six-row mismatch; demote “decisive proof of a
+restriction beyond all printed premises” to `OPEN[MOH-PROGRAM-ARTIFACT]`.
+
+### Claim (6)
+
+**CONFIRMED for the charged arithmetic pipeline.**  The rerun reproduces
+1,692/1,189 and 670 UNI groups alive at some integer $N\ge6$.  It also gives
+589 UNI and 648 mixed groups in $6\le N\le16$; $D=48$ is killed by the
+knapsack; $D=66,78$ have no path-arithmetic skeleton; and no $D>100$ is empty
+through 200.  The requested raw/group/UNI counts are
+
+| $D$ | $V$ rows | groups | UNI alive $N\ge6$ |
+|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| 105 | 15 | 14 | 7 |
+| 108 | 206 | 125 | 87 |
+| 112 | 76 | 71 | 33 |
+| 117 | 7 | 7 | 4 |
+| 120 | 782 | 515 | 271 |
+
+For $48\le D\le200$ the total is 23,720 rows / 14,016 groups / 8,831 UNI
+alive at $N\ge6$.  The $121\le D\le200$ increment is 22,028 / 12,827 /
+8,161.  The divisor-chain proof of $s\le5$ at $n\le100$ is correct, and the
+first charged $s=6$ witness occurs at $D=192$.  Promote these as baseline
+measurements only.  They cease to be “no-emptiness” results after the
+source-derived whole-tree filter: §4.5 shows many new empty degrees, including
+$D=105$ and $117$.
