+## 6. OPENs raised (bounded ledger)
+
+### `OPEN[MOH-PROGRAM-ARTIFACT]`
+
+Recover the CDC 6500 source, a faithful listing, or an independently preserved
+run, and decide whether p.202 records an unprinted predicate, an implementation
+shortcut, or an incomplete/incorrect output claim.  The bounded present
+residual at $n\le100$ is exactly **49 excess rows / 32 excess groups** after
+`C_FULL_TREE_PASSPORT`.  Those rows occupy
+
+```text
+(72,48), (80,32), (84,56), (90,60),
+(96,64), (96,72), (96,80), (100,80),
+```
+
+where $(84,56)$ is also one of the four printed degree classes; the total
+survivor union is 55 rows / 37 groups / 11 classes, hence seven new classes.
+The rejected and surviving witnesses are exhaustively certified in the
+`full-tree-passport-*-witnesses.json` artifacts.  At $48\le D\le200$ the
+corresponding bound is 2,581 rows / 1,261 groups / 803 pinned-$N$ groups.
+
+### `OPEN[FULL-TREE-RECENTER]`
+
+Prove or refute that Prop.5.4's polynomial-removable recentering step applies
+independently to every integral nonpositive-radius sibling in the recursively
+constructed factor tree.  Moh proves it only for the specially chosen
+globally smallest $gT_1$ disc, so promoting it edgewise would change a
+quantifier.  Its bounded effect at $n\le100$ is **at most 35 additional rows,
+25 groups, and four classes**: 55/37/11 becomes 20/12/7, with 14 excess rows
+in seven groups and exactly three new classes,
+
+```text
+(90,60), (96,64), (96,72).
+```
+
+At $48\le D\le200$ it changes 2,581/1,261/803 to
+1,315/631/429.  Even a proof would not close `OPEN[MOH-PROGRAM-ARTIFACT]`.
+
+The ordered audit of the user's candidate families is now:
+
+1. **(i) Prop.5.3:** a new restriction was found and promoted locally: the
+   whole tree, not one orbit-size path.  Remaining: simultaneous coefficient
+   and root-position compatibility of all sibling polynomials.
+2. **(ii) Prop.5.5:** excluded as a source of a second universal $r=2$
+   congruence; pp.187--188 give exactly (12)/(13), and the later inequality
+   is special to the contradiction then under study.
+3. **(iii) Prop.5.6:** resolved as typed `not all zero factors`, not the
+   numerical `NOT-ALL-(11)` shadow and not a new $A_1$ bit.  The arbitrary-
+   sibling recenter extrapolation remains `OPEN[FULL-TREE-RECENTER]`.
+4. **(iv) Section 6:** excluded as an additional scalar screen.  The strict
+   top split and top radius are automatic on all 658 rows; the other uses are
+   geometric or feed the already encoded tree capacities.
+5. **(v) Appendix II:** excluded as the pre-table program discriminator.  It
+   follows the p.202 output statement and performs case-specific eliminations
+   of those six rows; only the $(15,10;M_2=11,V_2=3)$ row receives the full
+   $2,2,6$ root-split contradiction on pp.210--211.
+6. **(vi) semigroup:** the correctly indexed Prop.3.1 bounded representation
+   is automatic on all 658 rows and all 23,720 degree-200 rows.  Every tested
+   stronger index/orientation that cuts substantially fails closed by killing
+   printed rows.  No conductor or approximate-root theorem imposing the
+   demanded cut was found in the audited source.
+
+For mathematical progress, remaining candidates rank: (1) simultaneous
+$f$/$g$ coefficient and root-position compatibility across the whole tree,
+explicitly identified as the unresolved interaction in Moh's introduction
+(p.143, final paragraph); (2) the edgewise-recenter quantifier; (3) a stronger
+but correctly indexed semigroup-realizability theorem not present in this
+paper.  For the historical question “what did the program execute?”, the
+lost listing or an incomplete/table-error explanation outranks all inferred
+mathematics.
