+## 5. Typed verdict block and promotion recommendations
+
+### 5.1 The theorem actually found
+
+**PROVED-IN-SOURCE (local whole-tree obligation).**  At a major disc $D_j$,
+write the common leading polynomial as $p(\pi)$ and let $u$ be the
+multiplicity of any one of its factors.  If
+
+\[
+             u>{d_j\over n-M_j},
+\]
+
+then that factor defines another major disc and its characteristic data must
+satisfy the same construction at the next level.  This applies to *every*
+such factor, not just to the factor chosen for the displayed $V$-path.  At
+the bottom, Prop.5.6 rules out the typed case in which every continuation is
+the zero factor.  Moh's proof is Prop.5.3, pp.181--185 (factor construction,
+root multiplicities, and the new major disc), Prop.5.6, pp.188--189 (pure
+point exclusion), and the recursive tree description on p.200, second and
+third paragraphs.
+
+`C_FULL_TREE` is the finite arithmetic consequence of that theorem.  It is
+uniform in $D$, not case-by-case: it cuts 658 rows to 60 while retaining all
+six printed rows, and gives exactly Moh's two rows at $(75,50)$.  The local
+differential identity in Appendix I, p.205, and the cyclic-orbit passport
+sharpen it source-safely to 55 rows.  The passport inequality is derived
+from Moh's equations, however; it is not a theorem that Moh states or says
+his program used.
+
+**PROVED-IN-SOURCE (the exact 652-row discriminator): NONE FOUND.**  No
+source-proved predicate tested here has survivor set equal to the p.202
+table.  It would therefore be false to type either `C_FULL_TREE_PASSPORT` or
+the 20-row exploratory screen as the missing program condition.
+
+### 5.2 Typed claim verdicts
+
+```text
+CLAIM (1)  CONFIRMED-WITH-REPAIR
+  Promote: the image transcription, symbol dictionary, and p.188 divisibility.
+  Repair: p(pi) is node-local; M4=n-1 can be a displayed successor, not an
+          effective searched datum.
+
